---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---
<Legal
  title="privacy policy"
  updated={site.legal.updated}
  meta="applies to · loggoo for ios and android"
  description="loggoo keeps your photos, notes and moods on your device. no account, no ads, no data selling — only anonymous crash and usage diagnostics."
>
  <div class="legal__panel">
    <h2>the short version</h2>
    <ul class="legal__checks">
      <li>your photos, notes and moods stay on your device. we cannot see them.</li>
      <li>no account, so we hold no name, email or profile for you.</li>
      <li>we collect anonymous, aggregated usage and crash data to fix what breaks.</li>
      <li>no ads, no ad sdks, no selling or sharing of your data. ever.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>1 · who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    {site.studio} is the data controller for the limited data described here. contact:
    <a href={'mailto:' + site.email}>{site.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>2 · what stays on your device</h2>
  <p>
    everything you log — photos taken in or imported into loggoo, mood entries, notes, streak history and frames you
    generate — is written to your device's local storage. it is not uploaded to any loggoo server, because we do not run
    one for user content. camera and photo library permissions are requested only when you use those features, and can be
    withdrawn in your device settings at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>3 · optional cloud sync and backup</h2>
  <p>
    if you switch on backup or sync, loggoo stores an encrypted copy of your log in <strong>your own</strong> icloud or
    google drive account so you can restore it on a new device. that copy lives under your cloud account, governed by
    apple's or google's privacy policy. we have no access to it and cannot read, restore or delete it on your behalf.
    switching the setting off stops future uploads; removing the existing copy is done from your cloud account.
  </p>

  <h2>4 · what we do collect</h2>
  <p>to keep the app working we collect anonymous, aggregated diagnostics that are not linked to your identity:</p>
  <ul class="legal__items">
    <li>
      <strong>crash and error reports</strong> — device model, os version, app version, and the technical stack trace of
      the failure.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>feature counters</strong> — for example "a frame was exported" or "a mood was logged", as counts only.
      never the photo, the note text or the mood value tied to a person.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>purchase validation</strong> — the receipt token from apple or google needed to confirm a pack you bought,
      plus the store country.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    we do not collect your name, email, phone number, contacts, precise location or advertising identifiers. we do not
    attempt to re-identify anonymous data.
  </p>

  <h2>5 · notifications</h2>
  <p>
    the daily reminder is a local notification scheduled on your device at the hour you choose. it does not travel
    through our servers and carries no content about your log. turn it off in loggoo's settings or in your device's
    notification settings.
  </p>

  <h2>6 · purchases</h2>
  <p>
    in-app purchases are processed entirely by the apple app store or google play. we never receive your payment card,
    billing address or full store account details — only the receipt needed to unlock what you bought and to let you
    restore it later.
  </p>

  <h2>7 · service providers we use</h2>
  <p>
    we use a small number of processors strictly for the purposes above: apple and google (app distribution, payments,
    and — at your choice — cloud storage), and a mobile crash-reporting and analytics provider that processes anonymous
    diagnostics on our behalf. they may not use that data for their own advertising. we do not sell or share personal
    information, and we have never received a legal request for user content — if that changes we will disclose what the
    law allows us to disclose.
  </p>

  <h2>8 · legal bases (eea / uk)</h2>
  <p>
    where the gdpr applies, we rely on: <strong>contract</strong> — to deliver the app and the purchases you make;
    <strong>legitimate interests</strong> — to keep the app stable and secure through anonymous diagnostics; and
    <strong>consent</strong> — for camera, photo library, notifications and optional cloud backup, each of which you
    grant or withdraw yourself.
  </p>

  <h2>9 · your rights</h2>
  <p>
    you can delete every moment you have logged from settings → delete all data, and uninstalling loggoo removes the
    local database entirely. because your content never reaches us, deletion is immediate and complete on your side.
  </p>
  <p>
    under the gdpr you also have rights of access, rectification, erasure, restriction, portability and objection; under
    the ccpa/cpra, californian residents have rights to know, delete and correct, and to opt out of sale or sharing — we
    do not sell or share personal information, so there is nothing to opt out of. we do not discriminate against anyone
    who exercises these rights. write to <a href={'mailto:' + site.email}>{site.email}</a> and we will respond within 30
    days; note that anonymous diagnostics may not be identifiable enough for us to isolate your specific records.
  </p>

  <h2>10 · retention</h2>
  <p>
    your log stays on your device until you delete it. anonymous crash and usage data is retained in aggregate for up to
    14 months, then discarded. purchase receipts are retained as long as needed to honour restores and to meet tax and
    accounting duties.
  </p>

  <h2>11 · children</h2>
  <p>
    loggoo is not directed to children under 13 (or the minimum age in your country), and we do not knowingly collect
    their data. loggoo has no social features, no public content and no messaging.
  </p>

  <h2>12 · security and international transfers</h2>
  <p>
    local data is protected by your device's own encryption and lock screen; keeping a passcode on your phone is the
    single most effective protection for your log. the limited anonymous data we receive may be processed on servers
    outside your country under standard contractual clauses or equivalent safeguards. no method of storage or
    transmission is perfectly secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.
  </p>

  <h2>13 · changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    if this policy changes materially, we will update the date above and flag it in the app release notes before the
    change takes effect.
  </p>

  <div class="legal__contact">
    <h2>14 · contact</h2>
    <p>
      privacy questions, data requests, or anything that reads wrong here:
      <a href={'mailto:' + site.email}>{site.email}</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Legal>
